	"web_text": "Mythological subjects for fans as well as paintings were first favored in Italy but became widely popular with increased travel to the country by well-heeled Europeans on Grand Tours. Fan leaves of Italian provenance were often ornamented with images of celebrated paintings by Renaissance and Baroque artists such as Annibale Carracci, Raphael, Guido Reni, and Giulio Romano. These could be purchased fully mounted or mounted in travelers' home countries, thus reducing import duties. This fan's leaf design is based upon Reni's famous painting of Bacchus, the Roman god of agriculture, wine, and fertility, and his consort, Ariadne.",
	"didactic_label": "Mythological subjects for fans as well as paintings were first favored in Italy but became widely popular with increased travel to the country by well-heeled Europeans on Grand Tours. Fan leaves of Italian provenance were often ornamented with images of celebrated paintings by Renaissance and Baroque artists such as Annibale Carracci, Raphael, Guido Reni, and Giulio Romano. These could be purchased fully mounted or mounted in travelers' home countries, thus reducing import duties. This fan's leaf design is based upon Reni's famous painting of Bacchus, the Roman god of agriculture, wine, and fertility, and his consort, Ariadne.",
